From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 16:23:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] module env: drop writes to indirect bindings instead of
 panicking

Assignment that resolves to an indirect (re-exported) module binding is
a page-level error that V8 surfaces as a catchable TypeError. boa
panics here, and the panic unwinds through the whole wasm boundary.
Real sites trip this intermittently.

ModuleEnvironment::set returns (), and threading JsResult through
DeclarativeEnvironment::set's many callers would be an invasive change.
Drop the write instead. The correct upstream fix is to throw a
TypeError.
---
 src/environments/runtime/declarative/module.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/environments/runtime/declarative/module.rs b/src/environments/runtime/declarative/module.rs
index bd6df7f..56eaf1b 100644
--- a/src/environments/runtime/declarative/module.rs
+++ b/src/environments/runtime/declarative/module.rs
@@ -115,8 +115,8 @@ impl ModuleEnvironment {

         match &mut bindings[index as usize] {
             BindingType::Direct(v) => *v = Some(value),
-            BindingType::Indirect(_) => {
-                panic!("cannot modify indirect references to other environments")
-            }
+            // Writing an indirect (re-exported) binding is a page error V8
+            // reports as a TypeError. Ignore the write rather than panic.
+            BindingType::Indirect(_) => {}
         }
     }
